    "description": "**Description**\n\n\n### **Description**\n\n  \n\nWhy Norstella? Norstella unites market\\-leading companies that all have a shared goal of improving patient access. Each organization (Citeline, Evaluate, MMIT, Panalgo, and The Dedham Group) delivers must\\-have answers for critical strategic and commercial decision\\-making.\n  \n\n  \n\nTogether, we help our clients:* Assess the market need and competitive landscape\n* Know precisely which drugs to prioritize in their portfolio\n* Find out where the launch difficulties will be\u2014before they\u2019re difficulties\n* Track and improve market access post\\-launch\n\n  \n\nBy combining the efforts of each organization under Norstella, we can offer an even wider breadth of expertise, cutting\\-edge data solutions and expert advisory services alongside advanced technologies such as real\\-world data, machine learning and predictive analytics. At Norstella, we don\u2019t just deliver information and insights. We deliver answers you can act on. **Real World Data Consulting Lead**\n\n\nSenior Director / Vice President \u2022 Norstella \u2022 Remote (US)\n\n  \n\n**Function**\n\n  \n\nRWD Services and Consulting Practice Lead\n\n **Level**\n\n  \n\nVP, RWD Consulting\n\n **Location**\n\n  \n\nRemote \u2013 United States\n\n **Revenue Scope**\n\n  \n\n$10M P\\&L; 25% year\\-over\\-year growth target\n\n **Reports To**\n\n  \n\nSVP MA Services\n\n **Team**\n\n  \n\nGrowing consulting practice (current \\+ planned hires)\n\n### **THE OPPORTUNITY**\n\n\nWe are seeking a leader to build and scale Norstella\u2019s Real World Data consulting practice. This practice focuses on supporting both commercial and HEOR use cases to provide meaningful insights to our customers leveraging the Norstella RWD data assets. This is a high\\-impact role for a leader who combines deep RWD expertise with a commercial mindset. You will define the service offerings, partner with our commercial team, drive service excellence, provide our customers with meaningful insights, and grow a world\\-class team. You will serve as the senior\\-most expert and executive sponsor for our largest clients. This role owns a $10M revenue line with a mandate to drive 25% year\\-over\\-year growth through a combination of account expansion and collaboration with commercial sales team to grow consulting/services business.  \n\n\n\n  \n\n### **KEY RESPONSIBILITIES**\n\n**Practice Leadership \\& Strategy**\n\n* Define and execute the multi\\-year vision and go\\-to\\-market strategy for Norstella\u2019s RWD services.\n* Build and continuously innovate the consulting service portfolio\u2014spanning commercial and provider analytics, evidence generation, and advanced analytics.\n* Serve as internal champion for RWD methodology and scientific excellence, ensuring rigor and fast time to value across all client engagements\n* Partner with Norstella\u2019s product, data, and technology teams to integrate proprietary data assets into differentiated consulting solutions\n\n**Revenue Growth \\& Commercial Execution**\n\n* Own the $15M consulting P\\&L with accountability for achieving 25% year\\-over\\-year revenue growth and achieve contribution margin targets.\n* Drive land\\-and\\-expand strategy\u2014securing new clients through consultative selling and deepening wallet share within existing accounts\n* Develop trusted, executive\\-level relationships with our clients, serving as a strategic advisor rather than a transactional vendor\n* Collaborate with our commercial team to co\\-lead the development of proposals, capability presentations, and responses to RFPs across the full business development lifecycle\n* Collaborate with Norstella\u2019s commercial team to align sales motions, identify cross\\-sell opportunities, and build a healthy pipeline\n* Establish and track KPIs for revenue, margin, utilization, and client satisfaction; report progress to executive leadership\n\n**Delivery Excellence \\& RWD Leadership**\n\n* Oversee our existing verticals: commercial and provider analytics, evidence generation, and advanced analytics to provide differentiated capabilities by combining our Norstella data assets with meaningful insights and high\\-impact consulting and services deliverables.\n* Oversee the design and execution of high\\-quality RWD studies including retrospective cohort analyses, HEOR evaluations, comparative effectiveness research, and safety/epidemiology studies\n* Provide services that offer high\\-impact meaningful insights to commercial analytics with fast time to value to serve multiple use cases such as: HCP targeting, patient journey, patient finding, brand performance, launch analytics, and more.\n* Ensure methodological rigor and regulatory defensibility across all deliverables, particularly for FDA RWE submissions and HTA dossiers\n* Drive innovation in analytical approaches\u2014incorporating machine learning, NLP, and AI\\-driven methods where they add meaningful client value\n* Lead quality review of key deliverables; maintain accountability for client outcomes and satisfaction\n* Cultivate and leverage Norstella\u2019s data assets (claims, EHR, specialty pharmacy, oncology registries, etc.) to create differentiated evidence and commercial solutions\n\n**People Leadership \\& Culture**\n\n* Recruit, develop, and retain a high\\-performing team of RWD consultants, analysts, and scientific experts\n* Establish a culture of innovation, intellectual curiosity, and client\\-centricity within the practice\n* Leverage staffing models, capacity planning, and performance management processes for optimal business performance.\n* Foster strong cross\\-functional collaboration with Norstella\u2019s RWD data science and data delivery, market access, commercial and product teams\n\n**Thought Leadership \\& Market Presence**\n\n* Represent Norstella at industry conferences (ISPOR, ASCO) through presentations, panels, and publications\n* Author white papers, case studies, and points\\-of\\-view that establish Norstella as a leading voice in RWD/RWE\n* Engage with regulatory agencies, key opinion leaders, and payer stakeholders to shape the broader RWE conversation\n* Build and maintain an external network of academic collaborators, KOLs, and data partners\n\n### **QUALIFICATIONS**\n\n**Required**\n\n* Advanced degree in a relevant discipline (PhD, MD, PharmD, ScD, or MPH preferred; MBA with strong scientific background considered)\n* 12\\+ years of progressive experience in real\\-world data, health economics \\& outcomes research (HEOR), commercial analytics, epidemiology, or life sciences consulting\n* Demonstrated P\\&L ownership or significant revenue responsibility in a consulting, analytics, or professional services environment\n* Proven track record of growing client accounts and winning new business\u2014comfortable operating as scientist, commercial executive, and a seller\n* Deep expertise in RWD sources: claims (commercial, Medicare, Medicaid), EHR, specialty pharmacy data, patient registries, and linked datasets\n* Strong knowledge of regulatory frameworks for real\\-world evidence (FDA RWE Action Plan, PCORI methodology standards, NICE DSU guidance)\n* Experience designing and overseeing observational studies: cohort design, propensity score methods, IPTW, survival analysis, indirect treatment comparisons\n* Experience leading and developing multi\\-disciplinary teams of 10\\+ people\n* Exceptional executive communication and presentation skills; able to translate complex analytics into compelling business narratives\n\n**Preferred**\n\n* Experience at a top\\-tier life sciences consulting firm, CRO, Commercial Analytics, HEOR consultancy, or analytics company (e.g., IQVIA, Evidera, Analysis Group, Avalere)\n* Therapeutic area depth in oncology, rare disease, immunology, or neuroscience\n* Familiarity with AI/ML applications to RWD, including NLP for unstructured EHR data and predictive modeling\n* Existing relationships with senior decision\\-makers at top 20 pharmaceutical and biotech companies\n\n### **LEADERSHIP COMPETENCIES**\n\n\nWe are looking for a leader who embodies the following:\n\n* Entrepreneurial Drive \u2013 you see white space, build things from scratch, and are energized by building a business, not just managing one\n* Scientific Credibility \u2013 clients trust your expertise; you earn it through rigor, intellectual honesty, and staying close to the science\n* Commercial Analytics \u2013 clients trust you expertise to help guide impactful commercial decisions that find and reach patients quickly\n* Commercial Instinct \u2013 you understand what clients need before they articulate it, and you can translate that into a winning engagement or proposal\n* Creative Problem\\-Solving \u2013 you approach evidence challenges with ingenuity, designing novel analytical approaches where standard methods fall short\n* People Magnets \u2013 you attract and develop talent, and your teams consistently outperform because of the culture you create\n* Executive Presence \u2013 you are equally at home presenting to a pharma CMO, testifying to a payer panel, or mentoring a first\\-year analyst\n\n  \n\n  \n\n*Norstella is an equal opportunity employer. All job applicants will receive equal treatment regardless of race, creed, color, religion, alienage or national origin, ancestry, citizenship status, age, physical or mental disability or handicap, medical condition, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy\\-related conditions), marital or domestic partner status, military or veteran status, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, reproductive health decision making, or any other protected characteristic as established by federal, state, or local law.*  \n\n  \n\n*All legitimate roles with Norstella will be posted on Norstella\u2019s job board which is located at norstella.com/careers. If a role is not posted on this job board, a candidate should assume the role is not a legitimate role with Norstella. Norstella is not responsible for an application that may be submitted by or through a third\\-party and candidates should proceed with extreme caution if a third\\-party approaches them about an open role with Norstella. Norstella will never ask for anything of value or any type of payment during or as part of any recruitment, interview, or pre\\-hire onboarding process. If you are aware of or have reason to believe a job posting purportedly for a role with Norstella is fraudulent or otherwise not authorized by Norstella, please contact the Company using the following email address:* *ApplicationHelp@norstella.com*",
